From 15aa825283e8028a38b595d1e1043a212b25a881 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minpeter <62207008+minpeter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:23:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 107/111] sunxi: h713: h713_conlog - U-Boot's console for Linux
 on a board without a UART

With CONFIG_CONSOLE_RECORD, `h713_conlog <addr>` copies what U-Boot has
printed since relocation to <addr> behind a header ("H713CLOG", u32 length,
u32 flags), so that bootcmd can leave it on the eMMC:

  h713_disp init ${h713_project} logo; h713_conlog 0x45000000; mmc dev 1;
  mmc write 0x45000000 0x2800 0x400; run boot_${h713_boot}

The HY320 has no serial console on its one unit; this is how its first
boots were read (69 lines from Core: to "display initialised").
hy320_defconfig sets CONSOLE_RECORD with a 256 KiB buffer.
